    "claims: Regular weekly Thursday 08:30 ET dates are inferred from DOL's standing weekly rule (verified: false). The 3 holiday-shifted Wednesday dates (2026-11-25 Thanksgiving, 2027-11-10 Veterans Day, 2027-11-24 Thanksgiving) are explicitly published by DOL/ETA and marked verified: true.",
    "eia: Regular weekly Wednesday 10:30 ET dates are inferred from EIA's standing weekly rule (verified: false). The 6 holiday-shifted Thursday 12:00 ET dates in 2027 (Jan 21 MLK, Feb 18 Presidents, Jun 3 Memorial, Jul 8 Independence observed, Sep 9 Labor, Oct 14 Columbus) are explicitly published on eia.gov/petroleum/supply/weekly/schedule.php and marked verified: true.",
    "fomc / fomc_pc: Per federalreserve.gov tentative 2027 FOMC schedule, Oct 26-27, 2027 is dedicated to broad monetary policy strategy issues with no standard rate decision statement, and Nov 16-17, 2027 is the final scheduled rate-setting meeting of 2027 (no December 2027 meeting). Therefore 2027 has 7 rate-decision statements/press conferences (8 total including Dec 2026).",
    "fomc_min: Exact release dates of future FOMC Minutes are not pre-tabulated on federalreserve.gov; dates are inferred from the official Federal Reserve rule (Wednesday 14:00 ET, exactly 3 weeks after each rate-setting meeting) and marked verified: false. Minutes timing for the Oct 26-27, 2027 strategy meeting is not yet specified by the Fed and is omitted.",
    "ism_mfg / ism_svc: December 2026 dates (2026-12-01, 2026-12-03) are verified from ISM's 2026 schedule (verified: true). ISM's official 2027 calendar table has not yet been published on ismworld.org; 2027 dates are inferred from ISM's standing 1st/3rd business day rule (excluding weekends and US federal holidays) and marked verified: false. Note: ISM occasionally shifts the January release by 1 extra day if ISM observes an internal post-New Year holiday (e.g., Jan 4 -> Jan 5, 2027); verify once ISM posts its 2027 calendar."
